&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Working hours&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 While we are an all-remote company and hire&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/How-we-engage-talent-outside-of-the-US-218f7193695a46cbb1ef39ef9c1f72d4&quot;&gt; almost anywhere&lt;/a&gt; in the world, we do require successful candidates to be located in the United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred location:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every engineering organization has bought coding agents. Yet very few can confidently tell you that they’re making the impact they thought they would. They are falling short, not because the model isn’t good enough, but because the codebase is too complex and, outside of a few thousand people employed by OpenAI and Anthropic, nobody understands what &lt;em&gt;good&lt;/em&gt; context looks like. Agents can’t access all the code they need, they burn tokens hunting for the right code, and fill the gaps by guessing. Organizations build internal harnesses and knowledge bases using techniques that are outdated before the product is even in use. You’ll be the person to show customers how to actually fix these problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph gives the largest, most sophisticated engineering organizations in the world full codebase context so their teams and their agents can understand, oversee, and change their codebase with confidence. As agent adoption grows, and agents write more code, having the right context matters more and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being a brand new role, you’ll be building from scratch. You’ll define what the AI maturity curve looks like inside of enterprise organizations, turn that into a framework customers can use to assess themselves against, and lead engagements with customers where you’ll directly dig into their environment, build an action plan, and work with them to action it. Then you’ll measure again and show what changed and the results they’ve achieved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll spend your time in customer environments, in the room with VPs of Engineering and staff engineers, and in the product. You’ll also shape the broader market’s view on what good context looks like for agents, which is a question the whole industry is still figuring out. Your results will show up in how customers use the Sourcegraph platform and in the ways they are able to actually make agents work in enterprise codebases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across Sales, Field Engineering, Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, Marketing, and Product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn our products, our value prop, and how our largest customers use Sourcegraph&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shadow customer calls and interview customers about where their agents succeed and fail today&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review our existing benchmark studies and draft a first point of view on the dimensions of context that matter most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one quarter, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish Sourcegraph’s first perspective on context maturity, grounded in what you’ve learned from customer conversations and our own data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship v1 of the maturity framework: the categories, the criteria that define each stage, and how evidence maps to a score&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing to launch a self-serve version&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip Solutions Engineers to run a lightweight version of the assessment inside of trials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run your first assessment with 1-2 select customers, and refine the framework based on what you find&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅&lt;/strong&gt; Within six months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a recognized voice on context and agent readiness, with a steady cadence of writing, talks, or research that engineering leaders reference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish findings from real assessments: what you’re seeing across enterprise codebases, where agents break, and what moves the needle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a repeatable paid engagement with a defined scope, deliverables, and readout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver action plans that customers execute with you — activating workflows, integrations, and agentic use cases in their own environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Re-measure your first customers and show movement up the curve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed what you learn back to EPD as a standing input on agent effectiveness in the enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a consultant at heart, with technical chops and credibility. You can walk into a complex engineering organization, find what’s broken, and leave with a plan people act on. You’re equally comfortable telling a VP of Engineering their environment isn’t where they think it is as you are debating a staff engineer on why.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You build things that didn’t exist before: frameworks, practices, points of view. You can turn insight into action and you’re energized by a blank page as a starting point.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finally, you’re in the middle of the AI shift yourself. You have deep experience and strong opinions on where agents work and where they don’t, and you share them publicly. You stay on top of AI development, use new models and harnesses as they’re released, and have a perspective on how every generation of these products changes the story.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your skill-set:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years experience advising enterprise technology or engineering organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems or solutions architecture experience in large-scale software, the developer ecosystem, or SDLC environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI coding agents and a point of view on how enterprises are adopting them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating structured, repeatable approaches to diagnosing problems, such as frameworks, assessments, playbooks, or methodologies others can use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning technical findings into an executive-ready business roadmap, then working hands-on with customers to deliver it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve run your own consulting practice or built a consultative services offering from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in developer tooling, platform engineering, developer experience, or DevOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A public voice - writing or speaking - you have a body of work people reference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with consumption or usage-based products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
