&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership&lt;/strong&gt; — You own a process from source data through the financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curiosity&lt;/strong&gt; — You keep asking why until you find the system behind the break.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A data-backed voice&lt;/strong&gt; — You bring findings and recommendations to business owners with numbers behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical AI use&lt;/strong&gt; — You apply AI to speed up accounting work, with documented human review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Controller on the monthly and quarterly close in FloQast, tracking deadlines and sign-offs, and help shorten the close through process improvements and AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve journal entries and reconciliations prepared by others on the accounting team, including cash, accounts receivable, prepaids, deferred commissions, fixed assets, accruals, deferred revenue, and payroll liabilities, and propose the bad debt reserve for Controller approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft the monthly flux analysis with root-cause explanations for material variances, assemble the close review folder, and support the Controller in the review with the VP Finance and CFO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Senior Revenue Manager with revenue recognition (ASC 606), including deferred revenue, overage accruals, and usage true-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review AP, card, and payroll accruals and entries to confirm liabilities are recorded completely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare audit schedules for our external auditors and help document and test close controls with the Controller.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the accountants who prepare the close, and apply AI tools to flux analysis, accrual review, and reconciliation matching with documented human review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of progressive accounting experience, including at least 2 years reviewing the work of others or managing accountants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in accounting, finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on month-end close experience at a SaaS company, including reviewing journal entries and reconciliations in an ERP such as NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US GAAP for the accounts you will review, including accruals and unrecorded liabilities, prepaids, fixed assets, and payroll and commission liabilities, with specific knowledge of the allowance for credit losses (ASC 326), capitalized sales commissions (ASC 340-40), and the evaluation of errors and their materiality (ASC 250)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting an external audit, including preparing schedules and responding to auditor requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A specific example of using AI to make an accounting process or the close more efficient, which you built or deployed, and what it changed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication with non-finance partners, and the judgment to know when to escalate to the Controller&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: CPA license (active or inactive) or a Big 4 or public accounting background; experience with NetSuite, FloQast, and usage-based billing; SOX or internal controls exposure; and remote-first company experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. Starting salary for this role is &lt;strong&gt;$105k–$122k USD&lt;/strong&gt; (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we’re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave, unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
