&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Invisible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is an Applied AI research company closing the gap between frontier models and the enterprise. We provide the platform infrastructure that makes AI work in production at scale: unify fragmented data, map complex processes, orchestrate and evaluate agents, and stand up hyper-personalized workflow applications fast for companies like Grubhub, Alliance Global, and Thomson Reuters. Where models fall short, we build RL environments and data to fix them. The result: a virtuous cycle between enterprise deployment and model training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized as Best Predictive Analytics Platform of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards, Invisible makes AI work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible&#39;s Data Lab works with leading AI companies to design and deliver the human data that advances model capabilities and measures performance. Our work spans the full frontier of AI training and evaluation—from supervised fine-tuning and preference data to benchmarks, red teaming, multimodal data, coding tasks, and agent environments. Solutions architects are at the center of this work, working with clients to define the problem and translating open-ended model development problems into scalable programs with sound methodology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Solutions Architect to bring technical depth, sharp commercial judgment, and a strong command of the rapidly evolving AI training and evaluation landscape. Embedded within an account team working with a major frontier AI lab, you will lead solution design for new opportunities&amp;nbsp; and pilots. You will partner with Project Leads who own execution, client management, and overall project outcomes, while remaining accountable for the integrity, feasibility, and scalability of the solution through handoff and early delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will often enter when a client&#39;s ask is still underspecified. Your job is to understand what they are really trying to achieve, translate that into a collection we can execute, and help the client and our teams make the right technical, methodological, and commercial choices. You will connect the perspectives of client researchers, program managers, Project Leads, experts, and engineers—bringing context that may not otherwise exist in the room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional infrastructure architecture role, nor is it primarily a project management role. It sits at the intersection of ML research, human data, product thinking, and client partnership. Success means teams make better decisions because you are involved: projects are framed correctly, solutions reflect the state of the art, and clients trust Invisible to understand where their work is going next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across a remarkable range of frontier AI problems, with direct exposure to the researchers and program leaders defining them. You will help determine how novel human-data programs should work before there is an established playbook, influence the products and systems used to deliver them, and build reusable ways of thinking that shape how Invisible approaches the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you live and breathe LLM training and evaluation, communicate with unusual clarity, and want your judgment to matter in the room, this role offers a rare combination of technical range, client proximity, and real-world impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip account teams with the technical and research context they need to fully understand client requests and make sound decisions about how to approach them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the solution design of new human-data projects and pilots, working with Project Leads from early discovery and scoping through the transition into execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with client research and program management stakeholders to interpret ambiguous requests, uncover the underlying objective, and turn it into a clear and executable approach. For technical POCs in particular, you may take the lead in the relationship alongside the Project Lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on methodology/best practices across supervised fine-tuning, preference data and RLHF, benchmarks and evaluations, red teaming, multimodal data, coding tasks, agent environments, and emerging approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape task design, annotation and evaluation workflows, quality and validation strategies, data structures, and the trade-offs between research value, feasibility, speed, scale, and expert experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the expert profiles a project requires, including the knowledge, experience, and judgment needed to produce credible data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring commercial judgment to early scoping, building rough-cut estimates of effort, expert supply, timeline, and cost so teams can test feasibility and shape viable proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to define the expert-facing interfaces and technical architecture that collections require, including workflows, APIs, data exchange patterns, synthetic testing, and validation mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype or test critical elements of a solution during discovery, while working with Engineering as the team responsible for production implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build alignment across clients, account leadership, Project Leads, Engineering, expert operations, and other internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay deeply current on LLM training, post-training, human data, benchmarks, and evaluation research, and translate new developments into practical implications for active and future client work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and share reusable mental models, patterns, and emerging best practices that raise the technical fluency and solutioning quality of the wider organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Required&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, demonstrable interest in how frontier AI models are trained, improved, and evaluated. You actively follow the space and can form your own views rather than simply repeat its vocabulary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of LLM training and evaluation concepts, with the ability to reason across data modalities, collection methods, and research objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills. You can listen closely, identify what is missing from an underspecified request, explain complex ideas clearly, and influence technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The judgment to challenge assumptions constructively while maintaining momentum and client trust. You know when to ask another question, when to recommend a different approach, and when to make a pragmatic call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical fluency in ML, data systems, software architecture, APIs, and data flows to collaborate credibly with researchers and engineers and to shape implementable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial judgment and comfort with rough-cut budgeting, particularly when weighing research ambition against expert availability, delivery effort, timeline, cost, and unit economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize client context, research intent, expert capabilities, user experience, technical constraints, and operational realities into an executable approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple stakeholders or teams, particularly in ambiguous environments where responsibilities and requirements continuously evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership, curiosity, adaptability, and low ego. You care more about reaching the right answer and improving the outcome than being the person who supplied it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in computer science, software engineering, machine learning, data science, AI research, technical product, solutions architecture, or a related field. Equivalent knowledge gained through independent work or other professional experience is equally welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with human-data programs, data annotation, model post-training, RLHF, RLVR, evaluations, benchmarks, red teaming, or research operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with AI researchers, research engineers, or technical program managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on ability with tools such as Python, SQL, APIs, notebooks, or lightweight prototyping. You will not be the primary builder, but being able to inspect, test, or demonstrate an idea can make you more effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing tools or workflows for specialized users, particularly where expert judgment and data quality are central to the outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of serious engagement with the field through professional work, research, open-source contributions, technical writing, independent projects, benchmark participation, or other forms of self-directed learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bonus and equity is included in all full-time, non commission offers. Final compensation is determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, internal pay equity, and overall market conditions. Because of this, every offer is unique. Additional details on total compensation and benefits will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can find more information about our geographic pay tiers&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; During the interview process, your Invisible Talent Acquisition Partner will confirm which tier applies to your location. For candidates outside the U.S., compensation is adjusted to reflect local market conditions and cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What It&#39;s Like to Work at Invisible:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Invisible, we’re not just redefining work—we’re reinventing it. We operate at the intersection of advanced AI and human ingenuity, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible to unlock productivity and scale. Ownership is at the core of everything we do. Here, you won’t just execute tasks—you’ll build, innovate, and shape the future alongside world-class clients pushing the boundaries of AI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We expect bold ideas, relentless drive, and the ability to turn ambiguity into opportunity. The pace is fast, the challenges are big, and the growth is unmatched. We’re not for everyone, and we’re okay with that. If you’re looking for predictable routines, this isn’t the place for you. But if you’re driven to create, thrive in dynamic environments, and want a front-row seat to the AI revolution, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;Invisible is a hybrid organization with offices and team members located around the world. While some roles may offer remote flexibility, most positions involve in-office collaboration and are tied to specific locations. Any location-based requirements or hybrid expectations will be communicated by our Talent Acquisition team during the recruiting process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;AI Interviewing Guidelines:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Our hiring team thoughtfully uses AI to support an efficient, engaging, and inclusive interview process. Since AI can also be a helpful tool for candidates, we&#39;ve outlined expectations for using it ethically throughout your interview journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Click here to learn more about how we use AI and our guidelines for candidates.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accessibility Statement:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(52, 73, 94);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. If you require an accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please submit your request using our &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation request form.&lt;/a&gt; A member of our team will follow up to support your request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Invisible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is an Applied AI research company closing the gap between frontier models and the enterprise. We provide the platform infrastructure that makes AI work in production at scale: unify fragmented data, map complex processes, orchestrate and evaluate agents, and stand up hyper-personalized workflow applications fast for companies like Grubhub, Alliance Global, and Thomson Reuters. Where models fall short, we build RL environments and data to fix them. The result: a virtuous cycle between enterprise deployment and model training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized as Best Predictive Analytics Platform of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards, Invisible makes AI work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Director of Engineering to set the technical strategy for Data Labs, the team that builds the benchmarking systems, data pipelines, and RL environments behind our AI training engagements. The frontier labs and enterprises we work with are changing how they train, evaluate, and deploy models every quarter. Your job is to see where that market is going and make sure Data Labs is built for it before our clients ask.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll decide which capabilities we invest in, which we standardize into platform, and which we leave to individual engagements. You&#39;ll track how training methods, evaluation practices, and data needs are shifting across the industry, and turn that into a technical roadmap and a point of view our commercial and research teams can sell against.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead a group of engineering managers, forward deployed engineers (FDEs), and senior ICs, and partner closely with applied research, product, and go-to-market leadership. This is a hands-on strategic role. You won&#39;t spend much time writing code, but you&#39;ll stay close enough to the technical work to make and defend hard architectural calls, and close enough to clients to know which calls matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Strategy &amp;amp; Roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-year technical strategy for Data Labs, and translate it into a roadmap tied to where the AI training and evaluation market is heading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide where to build shared platform versus engagement-specific solutions, weighing reuse against team autonomy so platforms speed teams up rather than creating over-dependency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set architectural direction for benchmarking infrastructure, data pipelines, and RL environments so they stay reproducible, portable across client deployments, and ready for the next generation of training methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate technical shifts 6–18 months out, such as new post-training techniques, agentic evaluation, and synthetic data, and place the bets that keep Invisible ahead of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set expectations for how AI is used in design reviews and day-to-day engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Competitive Positioning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a clear, current view of how frontier labs and enterprises are training, evaluating, and deploying models, and what that means for the data and infrastructure they&#39;ll need from us.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track the competitive landscape across AI data, evaluation, and RL environment providers, and help define where Invisible differentiates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn client signals, research developments, and market trends into investment recommendations for executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and commercial teams to shape new offerings, pricing logic, and the technical story behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluation &amp;amp; Data Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Invisible&#39;s point of view on benchmarking and evaluation, including pre- and post-engagement comparisons, capability gap analyses, and regression tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure evaluation design ties to client-defined success metrics, validate automated checks against human judgment, and be explicit about what each approach can&#39;t see.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify reusable data assets, frameworks, and pipelines that become durable advantages and improve margins across engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape practices for data licensing, privacy, and contamination risk as a strategic differentiator, not just a compliance requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client &amp;amp; Executive Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent engineering in executive conversations, strategic client relationships, and pre-sales, translating technical reality into clear, honest narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted technical advisor to client research and engineering leaders, bringing back what you learn to inform the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help leaders weigh client-specific asks against broader platform and business goals, with clear short- and long-term paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow an engineering org of multiple teams, including engineering managers, senior managers, FDEs, and Staff+ ICs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach managers to build sound technical judgment and strategic awareness in their teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build hiring pipelines that reinforce a rigorous, client-focused, strategy-aware engineering culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure the org has the planning, quality, and operational practices it needs to execute on the strategy reliably, delegating day-to-day delivery to strong managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in software engineering, with significant experience building ML or AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in engineering leadership, including experience managing managers across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting multi-year technical strategy and making platform investment decisions that paid off commercially.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, current understanding of the AI training and evaluation landscape, including how frontier labs and enterprises approach fine-tuning, RLHF/RLAIF, and evaluation methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on familiarity with LLM training pipelines, deep enough to make and defend architectural decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building benchmarking, data curation, or RL infrastructure that produced measurable client outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read market and competitive signals and turn them into a technical roadmap and a clear product point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional partnership with applied research, product, and commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive communication, and confidence acting as a technical advisor in client and pre-sales conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at an AI services firm, applied research consultancy, frontier lab, or enterprise AI product company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A visible point of view on the AI data and evaluation market, such as talks, writing, or open-source work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data licensing, synthetic data generation, or contamination detection involving client data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping new product lines or service offerings from a technical foundation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading an org through rapid growth or significant change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s In It For You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is committed to fair and competitive pay, ensuring that compensation reflects both market conditions and the value each team member brings. Our salary structure accounts for regional differences in cost of living while maintaining internal equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this position, the annual salary will include a 20% annual bonus and an additional incentive structure. The base salary range for SF/NY are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$252,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bonus and equity is included in all full-time, non commission offers. Final compensation is determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, internal pay equity, and overall market conditions. Because of this, every offer is unique. Additional details on total compensation and benefits will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can find more information about our geographic pay tiers&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; During the interview process, your Invisible Talent Acquisition Partner will confirm which tier applies to your location. For candidates outside the U.S., compensation is adjusted to reflect local market conditions and cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What It&#39;s Like to Work at Invisible:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Invisible, we’re not just redefining work—we’re reinventing it. We operate at the intersection of advanced AI and human ingenuity, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible to unlock productivity and scale. Ownership is at the core of everything we do. Here, you won’t just execute tasks—you’ll build, innovate, and shape the future alongside world-class clients pushing the boundaries of AI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We expect bold ideas, relentless drive, and the ability to turn ambiguity into opportunity. The pace is fast, the challenges are big, and the growth is unmatched. We’re not for everyone, and we’re okay with that. If you’re looking for predictable routines, this isn’t the place for you. But if you’re driven to create, thrive in dynamic environments, and want a front-row seat to the AI revolution, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;Invisible is a hybrid organization with offices and team members located around the world. While some roles may offer remote flexibility, most positions involve in-office collaboration and are tied to specific locations. Any location-based requirements or hybrid expectations will be communicated by our Talent Acquisition team during the recruiting process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;AI Interviewing Guidelines:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Our hiring team thoughtfully uses AI to support an efficient, engaging, and inclusive interview process. Since AI can also be a helpful tool for candidates, we&#39;ve outlined expectations for using it ethically throughout your interview journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Click here to learn more about how we use AI and our guidelines for candidates.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accessibility Statement:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(52, 73, 94);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. If you require an accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please submit your request using our &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation request form.&lt;/a&gt; A member of our team will follow up to support your request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Invisible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is an Applied AI research company closing the gap between frontier models and the enterprise. We provide the platform infrastructure that makes AI work in production at scale: unify fragmented data, map complex processes, orchestrate and evaluate agents, and stand up hyper-personalized workflow applications fast for companies like Grubhub, Alliance Global, and Thomson Reuters. Where models fall short, we build RL environments and data to fix them. The result: a virtuous cycle between enterprise deployment and model training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized as Best Predictive Analytics Platform of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards, Invisible makes AI work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a generalist People Experience role. You&#39;ll work across the whole People team, taking things from idea to delivered, reporting to the People Experience Director as their main support for execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A good part of the job is making the rest of the team better at what it does: streamlining People Operations processes, rewriting the policies behind them, and getting their projects over the line. The rest is content, programs, and employee relations casework of your own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have proper support around you. In-house legal counsel covers anything with real risk attached, and our People Operations specialists own the systems and transactional work. Your job is improving how it all runs, not carrying it alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content:&lt;/strong&gt; you write the competency frameworks, policies, guides, and comms the team needs and never has time to produce properly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programs:&lt;/strong&gt; you run projects end to end. You build the plan, chase the stakeholders, hold the dates, and get it across the line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Relations:&lt;/strong&gt; you run and manage cases yourself, start to finish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and policy:&lt;/strong&gt; you find what&#39;s clunky across the People team and fix it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Content creation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write competency frameworks, career paths, and leveling content for teams across Invisible, working from subject matter input from leaders and business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain policies. Own the handbook. Keep it accurate as we change entities, countries, and structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft internal comms for People team initiatives: announcements, manager guidance, FAQs, rollout messaging. You&#39;ll write in our voice, which is direct and short. Not corporate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the practical stuff that makes a program real: manager toolkits, training decks, process guides, templates, briefing docs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Program management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate People team programs end to end: performance cycles, engagement survey and action planning, onboarding improvements, platform rollouts, framework launches, compliance projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build project plans with owners, dates, and dependencies. Track them. Escalate early when something slips.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate stakeholders across People, Legal, Finance, Talent Acquisition, and business leadership. They don&#39;t report to you and all of them are busy. You still get the decisions you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the follow-through after decisions get made. The gap between &quot;we agreed this&quot; and &quot;this is live&quot; is your job to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Employee Relations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and manage ER cases: grievances, investigations, performance management, absence, conduct, exits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take cases from intake to outcome. Hold meetings, take notes, gather evidence, write up findings, draft outcome letters, keep records clean.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our in-house employment counsel and the Employment Relations team on anything complex or high risk. You&#39;re supported on the hard ones, and you&#39;re running the caseload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot patterns. If three cases in one team say the same thing, you say so.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Supporting People Operations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the processes behind our day-to-day: onboarding and offboarding, contract changes, leave, reference letters, ticket flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document what isn&#39;t documented and simplify what&#39;s grown complicated. If a process you just ran was painful, you rewrite it before the next cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help People Ops land their projects: system rollouts, audit and compliance prep, vendor changes, data cleanups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull and sanity-check data when someone needs a number to make a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You use AI to produce content fast and well.&lt;/strong&gt; You can take a messy brief and a few stakeholder conversations and come back with a framework or policy that is accurate, readable, and on tone. We care about the output and the judgment behind it, not how long it took.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US employee relations case management. Essential.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve run US cases independently, including investigations and performance exits. You know where the legal risk sits, how it shifts by state, and when to escalate. Exposure to other jurisdictions is a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A generalist track record in fast growth.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve worked in a generalist People or HR role at a startup or scale-up where the process didn&#39;t exist yet, and you were the person who actually delivered. You know what to build now and what can wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You finish things.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve project managed something with more than five stakeholders and landed it on time. You close the loop without being chased, and you flag risk early rather than explaining a miss afterward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You move people without authority.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll chase senior stakeholders for input and decisions. You&#39;re comfortable being politely relentless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re organized in a way other people can see.&lt;/strong&gt; Trackers, clear status, no surprises. If a program has six workstreams, you can tell us in 30 seconds where all six are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort with ambiguity.&lt;/strong&gt; Some briefs will be clear. Some will be a sentence and a deadline. You come back with a draft, not a list of questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; HRIS, spreadsheets, survey data. You can pull the numbers, sanity-check them, and put them in front of someone who needs to decide something.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed org experience.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re global and remote-first, across multiple time zones and entities. You know how to keep things moving asynchronously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You like breadth.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather do eight different things well than one thing forever, and you believe in evidence over instinct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re less interested in years of experience than in evidence you&#39;ve produced a lot of good work. Bring examples. Frameworks you wrote, programs you ran, cases you closed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$126,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$148,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bonus and equity is included in all full-time, non commission offers. Final compensation is determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, internal pay equity, and overall market conditions. Because of this, every offer is unique. Additional details on total compensation and benefits will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can find more information about our geographic pay tiers&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; During the interview process, your Invisible Talent Acquisition Partner will confirm which tier applies to your location. For candidates outside the U.S., compensation is adjusted to reflect local market conditions and cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What It&#39;s Like to Work at Invisible:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Invisible, we’re not just redefining work—we’re reinventing it. We operate at the intersection of advanced AI and human ingenuity, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible to unlock productivity and scale. Ownership is at the core of everything we do. Here, you won’t just execute tasks—you’ll build, innovate, and shape the future alongside world-class clients pushing the boundaries of AI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We expect bold ideas, relentless drive, and the ability to turn ambiguity into opportunity. The pace is fast, the challenges are big, and the growth is unmatched. We’re not for everyone, and we’re okay with that. If you’re looking for predictable routines, this isn’t the place for you. But if you’re driven to create, thrive in dynamic environments, and want a front-row seat to the AI revolution, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
