&lt;p&gt;Invisible is an Applied AI research company closing the gap between frontier models and the enterprise. We provide the platform infrastructure that makes AI work in production at scale: unify fragmented data, map complex processes, orchestrate and evaluate agents, and stand up hyper-personalized workflow applications fast for companies like Grubhub, Alliance Global, and Thomson Reuters. Where models fall short, we build RL environments and data to fix them. The result: a virtuous cycle between enterprise deployment and model training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized as Best Predictive Analytics Platform of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards, Invisible makes AI work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own IT at Invisible, an AI company that builds and deploys AI for frontier labs and enterprises. That gives you an opportunity most IT leaders don’t get: you have our AI tools and expertise in-house. You’ll design how agents and automation run IT, from onboarding and access management to device compliance and support, so a small team can serve a global remote workforce at scale. You will lead that team, run the operational controls that keep our people secure and productive, and take over vendor, contract and procurement management, where AI can speed up evaluation, renewals and spend decisions. This is a senior, hands-on leadership role. You’ll set the direction for IT, build the systems yourself, and show how AI changes what an IT function can do for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the IT function end to end: roadmap, budget, priorities and team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run vendor and contract management and procurement coordination. Own the renewals calendar, negotiations and spend visibility, working with Finance and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own identity and access management: Okta, Google Workspace, SSO, permissioning, and joiner, mover and leaver processes with People Experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage endpoints and the laptop fleet (currently Fleet), including provisioning, baselines and offboarding recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate corporate IT security controls day to day: monitor security tooling and alerts, manage password and secrets storage, and keep admin and owner access documented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Security team, which owns security engineering. Support SOC 2 controls, audits and customer security due diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the service desk (Jira Service Management) and use automation to triage tickets and workflows. Decide whether further headcount is needed as that work matures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain runbooks for access requests, onboarding and offboarding, and vendor management, so knowledge does not sit with one person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop IT team members and any consultants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and running IT in a SaaS or technology company. [8+ years in IT, 3+ leading people or a function.]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on depth in identity, endpoint management, SaaS administration and access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with vendor management, procurement and contract negotiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SOC 2 or similar compliance frameworks. Experience supporting regulated customers is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive operator with sound judgment, who communicates clearly with executives and operates independently without waiting to be asked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward automation over headcount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Based in or near New York; the rest of the team is global and remote.]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$158,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$186,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bonus and equity is included in all full-time, non commission offers. Final compensation is determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, internal pay equity, and overall market conditions. Because of this, every offer is unique. Additional details on total compensation and benefits will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can find more information about our geographic pay tiers&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; During the interview process, your Invisible Talent Acquisition Partner will confirm which tier applies to your location. For candidates outside the U.S., compensation is adjusted to reflect local market conditions and cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
