&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery &amp;amp; Scoping: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead concise, high-impact workshops that surface true business needs, define success metrics, and craft phased, right-sized scopes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Own the roadmap for internal developer platforms and tooling — understand what slows engineers down, and build products they actually want to adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Stewardship:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and own delivery timelines and OKRs, run stand-ups, clear blockers, coordinate directly with engineering teams to advance outcomes, and escalate early to keep work on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Act as the primary product point of contact for strategic enterprise clients, nurturing executive relationships and ensuring alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Enabled Solution Design: &lt;/strong&gt;Combine client context with Invisible’s AI toolkit to architect solutions using classical automation, GenAI, and human-in-the-loop approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement: &lt;/strong&gt;Document playbooks, mentor new analysts/PMs, and feed insights back into Invisible’s product and sales teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
